            <ArticleTitle>Paraduodenal hernia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>64-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Over a 10 year period, four patients with paraduodenal hernia were encountered. Two had small hernias that were incidental findings at the time of surgery for an unrelated abdominal condition; these were managed by suture closure of the neck of the sac. The other two patients presented with intestinal obstruction and are discussed here with a review of the literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
